              "body": "Hi Valerie, your blood count is mildly low at 11.6 and your iron stores (ferritin 14) are on the low side, which fits the iron deficiency you've had for a while. Please keep taking the ferrous sulfate every day, ideally with something containing vitamin C and away from coffee or tea. Kidney, liver, thyroid, sugar and cholesterol numbers are all normal, and the HIV and hepatitis C screens are negative. We'll recheck the blood count and ferritin in about six months."
            }
